1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,500
That hungry purr has a cry hidden inside.

2
00:00:02,500 --> 00:00:04,766
A purr is not one flat sound.

3
00:00:04,766 --> 00:00:10,000
It can carry a low rumble and,
sometimes, a higher, cry-like layer.

4
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:13,765
In 2009, researchers recorded
purrs from ten cats in two

5
00:00:13,765 --> 00:00:18,000
situations: ordinary purring and
purring while soliciting food.

6
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:22,000
The solicitation purrs held
a pronounced high-frequency

7
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:26,000
peak, averaging about 380
hertz, within a broader purr.

8
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:29,176
Fifty listeners heard both
recordings at equal volume.

9
00:00:29,176 --> 00:00:32,000
They rated the solicitation
purrs as more urgent

10
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:35,000
and less pleasant, even
when they did not own cats.

11
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:39,950
So the cry in the purr is
real, not a clever plan.

12
00:00:39,950 --> 00:00:45,000
It is one more way a cat
can get a human to listen.
